          "path": "_m/g/c/r/d/oundle-wp/100119-paine-s-almshouses-west.jpg",
          "filename": "100119 Paine's Almshouses West Street Oundle 4-10-20.jpg",
          "caption": "Grade II* early 17th century almshouses comprising two wings one with a datestone of 1753. The former almshouses now comprise Paine's Cottages on the east wing and the Manse of Oundle Congregational Church in the west wing; both are linked with an Elizabethan gateway. The wings were of a 15th century house, the bays being a later addition. The house now missing the central hall was owned by Sir Walter Mildmay of Apethorpe Hall, Chancellor to Elizabeth I.",
          "alt": "Grade II* early 17th century almshouses comprising two wings one with a datestone of 1753. The former almshouses now comprise Paine's Cottages on the east wing and the Manse of Oundle Congregational Church in the west wing; both are linked with an Elizabethan gateway. The wings were of a 15th century house, the bays being a later addition. The house now missing the central hall was owned by Sir Walter Mildmay of Apethorpe Hall, Chancellor to Elizabeth I.",
